The idea has merit in principle, but there is one key aspect...the size of
the god's name. A character whose god has a short name has a rather
distinct advantage because it is easier to gem-engrave in fewer turns, or
you could complete it with an edged weapon before it gets too dull.

The other thing is spelling...Mars is easy, Quetzalcoatl is not.

Then there's throwing out the whole Tolkeinesque reason for the E word,
where just speaking it out loud is enough to ward off the ringwraiths.
Since nethack doesn't let you speak, that wouldn't be viable (and if
Elbereth only works on purple W's, may as well remove it entirely).


